        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "The glass transition temperature $( T _ { \\mathrm { g } } )$of the pure polymer was measured with a Mettler 821 calorimetric system. Polymer sample was dried under reduced pressure in a vacuum oven prior to measurement. Dry nitrogen was used as purge gas and thermogram was measured in the range 308– 523 K at a scan rate of 20 $\\mathrm { K } \\mathrm { m i n } ^ { - 1 }$.",
        "table_locator": null
      },
      "confidence": {
